Subject: [PATCH] FCEA3LAB: friendlier input-file lookup (double-click on macOS)

On macOS (and Linux file managers) a double-clicked command-line program runs
in a terminal whose working directory is the home folder, not the program's
folder, so typing a case name that sits next to the program failed with
"Could not locate input file".

- If <name>.inp is not in the working directory, it is also looked up next
  to the executable and in its samples/ folder; the .out/.plt are then
  written next to that input.
- The typed name is cleaned like a path dropped into a terminal: surrounding
  quotes removed, backslash-escaped blanks ("My\ Folder") restored, tabs and
  trailing blanks trimmed. Dragging the .inp into the prompt now works.
- When the file is still not found, the working folder and the program folder
  that were searched are printed.
- The output file path is printed on the console.

New helpers get_cwd and clean_path_input in source/fcea3lab.F90.
The banner version is bumped to FCEA3LAB 1.1 (1.0 was distributed without this patch).
Solver numerics unchanged. Apply after 0003.

diff --git a/source/fcea3lab.F90 b/source/fcea3lab.F90
index 8444a14..a62ff3b 100644
